1
00:00:00,105 --> 00:00:01,105
MkvDrama.net

2
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:06,402
Oh, it's starting!

3
00:00:06,486 --> 00:00:07,570
Hurry!

4
00:00:12,909 --> 00:00:13,827
All right.

5
00:00:18,665 --> 00:00:21,000
<i>Well, a lot of stuff happened,</i>

6
00:00:21,084 --> 00:00:24,128
<i>but that's the thrill</i>
<i>of a live broadcast, right?</i>

7
00:00:24,212 --> 00:00:28,258
<i>Thank you for staying with us</i>
<i>until the very end today.</i>

8
00:00:28,842 --> 00:00:31,511
<i>-Goodbye for now!</i>
-Three, two, one…

9
00:00:32,428 --> 00:00:33,388
<i>Okay!</i>

10
00:00:34,264 --> 00:00:35,807
Good work, everyone!

11
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:36,724
Good work!

12
00:00:36,808 --> 00:00:38,059
Good work!

13
00:00:38,143 --> 00:00:40,436
Your improvisation was amazing.

14
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:43,314
-Doing this live, every time.
-It was really funny.

15
00:00:43,398 --> 00:00:44,524
You're a big help.

16
00:00:44,607 --> 00:00:45,692
Thank you.

17
00:00:45,775 --> 00:00:48,695
I'll see you at the party, right?
It's in your honor.

18
00:00:51,114 --> 00:00:52,240
Oh, excuse me.

19
00:01:04,377 --> 00:01:07,922
You're too intense, working on
these ideas until morning.

20
00:01:08,798 --> 00:01:10,049
You think so?

21
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:13,970
On the very day
of the live broadcast, no less.

22
00:01:18,141 --> 00:01:19,559
Mr. Amagi is coming through.

23
00:01:19,642 --> 00:01:21,311
-Good work.
-Thank you.

24
00:01:29,611 --> 00:01:31,696
I'm going to go greet the staff first.

25
00:01:31,779 --> 00:01:32,614
Okay.

26
00:01:35,158 --> 00:01:36,451
See you.

27
00:01:40,788 --> 00:01:43,041
Make sure to show up tonight, okay?

28
00:01:44,709 --> 00:01:45,793
Sure.

29
00:01:48,379 --> 00:01:51,341
I don't know what you're thinking, but…

30
00:02:00,642 --> 00:02:03,186
In an era where television
is in a recession,

31
00:02:03,269 --> 00:02:06,189
the reason we've come this far
is thanks to the performers,

32
00:02:06,272 --> 00:02:08,066
the staff members,

33
00:02:08,149 --> 00:02:11,361
and the sponsors who support us every day.

34
00:02:11,444 --> 00:02:14,989
I want to take this opportunity
to thank you from the bottom of my heart.

35
00:02:15,073 --> 00:02:18,034
Being loved for this long
is not to be taken for granted.

36
00:02:18,117 --> 00:02:20,203
KOICHI AMAGI: I WANT TO TALK

37
00:02:20,286 --> 00:02:22,956
Let's celebrate
along with former staff members,

38
00:02:23,039 --> 00:02:27,543
and many familiar faces
of past performers who are here today.

39
00:02:30,964 --> 00:02:33,341
It doesn't look like it's going to stop.

40
00:02:34,342 --> 00:02:36,719
Everyone, let's move inside for now!

41
00:02:36,803 --> 00:02:38,763
Sorry! Follow me, please.

42
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:39,681
Just here!

43
00:02:39,764 --> 00:02:42,767
Please be careful! It's slippery.

44
00:02:44,477 --> 00:02:45,395
Sorry!

45
00:02:46,104 --> 00:02:48,147
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

46
00:02:58,533 --> 00:02:59,826
Excuse me.

47
00:02:59,909 --> 00:03:01,452
-Here, sorry.
-Thank you.

48
00:03:01,536 --> 00:03:03,287
-Thank you.
-Yes.

49
00:03:05,748 --> 00:03:06,666
Hey.

50
00:03:06,749 --> 00:03:08,960
It's the 20th anniversary of <i>Yusata</i>.
Isn't that amazing?

51
00:03:09,544 --> 00:03:11,838
-That's the one with Koichi Amagi, right?
-Yes.

52
00:03:11,921 --> 00:03:14,549
Twenty years ago, I was four years old.

53
00:03:15,717 --> 00:03:18,886
Dr. Masumi, do you ever watch television?

54
00:03:21,055 --> 00:03:23,599
I do not watch it frequently,

55
00:03:23,683 --> 00:03:25,768
but I value making time for comedy.

56
00:03:25,852 --> 00:03:26,978
That's surprising.

57
00:03:27,562 --> 00:03:32,650
Laughing secretes oxytocin,
which alleviates stress and anxiety.

58
00:03:32,734 --> 00:03:35,486
Therefore, I deliberately
make time for laughter.

59
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:36,904
Wow.

60
00:03:36,988 --> 00:03:38,323
You should laugh more.

61
00:03:38,406 --> 00:03:39,574
Look who's talking.

62
00:03:39,657 --> 00:03:41,826
By the way, where is Dr. Honda?

63
00:03:41,909 --> 00:03:44,245
He's gone for a week
for an academic conference.

64
00:03:44,329 --> 00:03:45,913
That's awfully long.

65
00:03:45,997 --> 00:03:48,499
He seemed really
enthusiastic about it, though.

66
00:03:48,583 --> 00:03:51,419
Is that really just because of
the conference?

67
00:03:52,003 --> 00:03:52,837
Who knows?

68
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,131
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

69
00:03:55,214 --> 00:03:56,841
JAPAN NEWS

70
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:00,511
What?

71
00:04:01,262 --> 00:04:02,430
Is something wrong?

72
00:04:03,056 --> 00:04:04,307
Dr. Matsubara?

73
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:08,227
Understood, we will
head there immediately.

74
00:04:12,982 --> 00:04:16,110
It says Koichi Amagi has suddenly died.

75
00:04:17,111 --> 00:04:18,738
KOICHI AMAGI (55) DIES SUDDENLY

76
00:04:19,739 --> 00:04:20,698
What?

77
00:04:29,957 --> 00:04:31,417
POLICE

78
00:04:34,504 --> 00:04:36,464
Koichi Amagi, 55-year-old male.

79
00:04:36,547 --> 00:04:37,882
He is believed to have jumped

80
00:04:37,965 --> 00:04:42,512
during the 20th anniversary celebration
of the program held at the station.

81
00:04:42,595 --> 00:04:44,430
The first person to discover him

82
00:04:44,514 --> 00:04:47,642
was Kazuhiko Muto, who serves
as the head director for <i>Yusata</i>.

83
00:04:47,725 --> 00:04:49,143
Hearing a loud noise,

84
00:04:49,227 --> 00:04:51,312
he went out to check the situation,

85
00:04:51,396 --> 00:04:54,607
found Mr. Amagi after his fall,
and reported it.

86
00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:58,069
Where did the fall occur from?

87
00:04:59,028 --> 00:05:01,197
It is believed he fell from over there.

88
00:05:04,367 --> 00:05:07,120
Since no suicide note
was found at the scene,

89
00:05:07,203 --> 00:05:09,705
it is thought that he jumped on impulse.

90
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,463
Is something the matter, Doctor?

91
00:05:18,464 --> 00:05:21,300
For a jump from that height,

92
00:05:21,384 --> 00:05:23,386
the body is far too clean.

93
00:05:23,970 --> 00:05:26,180
The amount of bleeding
and external trauma is minimal.

94
00:05:27,181 --> 00:05:28,307
It doesn't add up.

95
00:05:28,391 --> 00:05:31,727
We have also received information
that he was mentally unstable.

96
00:05:46,576 --> 00:05:50,788
I wonder if he had some things going on
in private.

97
00:05:53,749 --> 00:05:57,795
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

98
00:06:03,301 --> 00:06:05,219
I see.

99
00:06:07,054 --> 00:06:10,057
So this time MEJ is
involved with Amagi's case.

100
00:06:13,686 --> 00:06:15,021
That is troublesome.

101
00:06:18,566 --> 00:06:20,193
When it's a case involving a celebrity,

102
00:06:20,276 --> 00:06:22,278
we have to take into account
public opinion,

103
00:06:22,361 --> 00:06:23,905
making it harder for us.

104
00:06:23,988 --> 00:06:26,490
Has a suicide note been found
on Amagi's body?

105
00:06:26,574 --> 00:06:28,075
Is foul play suspected?

106
00:06:28,159 --> 00:06:29,410
Were there any witnesses?

107
00:06:29,493 --> 00:06:31,746
It was a celebration for <i>Yusata</i>, right?

108
00:06:31,829 --> 00:06:33,664
We don't know anything yet!

109
00:06:33,748 --> 00:06:34,665
Yes?

110
00:06:37,293 --> 00:06:38,252
What?

111
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:51,849
Let's begin.

112
00:06:57,772 --> 00:07:00,608
The cause of death is traumatic shock.

113
00:07:01,108 --> 00:07:02,735
Abdominal internal bleeding

114
00:07:02,818 --> 00:07:05,863
and multiple fractures of the skull
and ribs were confirmed.

115
00:07:05,947 --> 00:07:07,865
Judging by the internal damage,

116
00:07:07,949 --> 00:07:10,535
it is certain that the body
sustained a powerful impact.

117
00:07:11,744 --> 00:07:14,997
But the external damage is minimal,
isn't it?

118
00:07:15,081 --> 00:07:19,252
Yes. This leaves room for doubt regarding
the findings of a suicide by jumping.

119
00:07:19,335 --> 00:07:23,339
It is as if only the interior of the body
experienced the fall.

120
00:07:23,422 --> 00:07:24,757
It doesn't add up.

121
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,883
Right.

122
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:29,303
Furthermore, there are numerous
linear marks on the arms and back

123
00:07:29,387 --> 00:07:32,598
that are not typically seen
in falls from great heights.

124
00:07:32,682 --> 00:07:35,268
And there is one more point of concern.

125
00:07:35,351 --> 00:07:36,769
What is it?

126
00:07:38,354 --> 00:07:42,149
A tongue bite wound located on the side.

127
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:45,194
It is true that in cases of jumping,

128
00:07:45,278 --> 00:07:48,030
the lower jaw moves rapidly
in the closing direction,

129
00:07:48,114 --> 00:07:50,366
and wounds usually appear at the front.

130
00:07:50,449 --> 00:07:52,535
Why would it be on the side?

131
00:07:53,911 --> 00:07:57,582
Additionally, there are old
fracture scars on the skull.

132
00:07:58,165 --> 00:08:00,251
Could these be connected to something?

133
00:08:00,334 --> 00:08:01,836
Right now, we do not know.

134
00:08:01,919 --> 00:08:05,423
But it is difficult to consider this
a simple case of jumping.

135
00:08:10,886 --> 00:08:12,972
Why are you in such a hurry?

136
00:08:13,431 --> 00:08:17,018
The higher-ups are telling us
to process this as having no foul play.

137
00:08:18,102 --> 00:08:19,228
What?

138
00:08:24,692 --> 00:08:27,111
What's going on?
The police are pulling out?

139
00:08:27,194 --> 00:08:29,655
Looking at the circumstances,
he simply jumped.

140
00:08:29,739 --> 00:08:32,241
Testimony said
that he had suicidal thoughts.

141
00:08:32,325 --> 00:08:34,410
MEJ is currently investigating that--

142
00:08:34,493 --> 00:08:36,537
Looking at the circumstances,

143
00:08:37,204 --> 00:08:38,998
it was just a suicide.

144
00:08:50,718 --> 00:08:52,511
If it isn't Ms. Dojima.

145
00:08:53,054 --> 00:08:54,263
You look well.

146
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,021
Please leave.

147
00:09:10,363 --> 00:09:11,864
<i>It's pressure from the higher-ups,</i>

148
00:09:11,947 --> 00:09:15,117
so I doubt even Ms. Dojima
can do anything about this.

149
00:09:20,623 --> 00:09:22,208
What should we do, Doctor?

150
00:09:44,522 --> 00:09:45,940
Mr. Muto,

151
00:09:46,023 --> 00:09:50,611
did you meet with Mr. Amagi
just before he passed away?

152
00:09:50,695 --> 00:09:53,447
Yes, briefly, to discuss the show.

153
00:09:53,531 --> 00:09:56,409
He sent me a message saying
he wanted to talk in private.

154
00:09:56,492 --> 00:09:57,535
I WANT TO TALK

155
00:10:02,957 --> 00:10:04,542
What did you want to talk about?

156
00:10:09,797 --> 00:10:11,841
There are many guests here today.

157
00:10:15,136 --> 00:10:17,555
You'll be fine even if I'm gone, right?

158
00:10:18,472 --> 00:10:19,390
What?

159
00:10:22,435 --> 00:10:24,019
I'm at my limit.

160
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:29,692
It gave me a bad feeling.

161
00:10:30,359 --> 00:10:32,903
Had he not consulted you
about anything before that?

162
00:10:32,987 --> 00:10:34,113
Never.

163
00:10:34,196 --> 00:10:36,991
Lately, we only had routine
work-related communications,

164
00:10:37,074 --> 00:10:39,994
mostly handled through his wife,
who acts as his manager.

165
00:10:42,163 --> 00:10:45,833
He really changed. He did.

166
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:50,588
Now, he's a nationwide star…

167
00:10:50,671 --> 00:10:51,714
Thank you.

168
00:10:51,797 --> 00:10:56,135
<i>…while we're just a small production</i>
<i>company riding on his coattails.</i>

169
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:59,513
<i>To him, I suppose this program</i>

170
00:11:00,681 --> 00:11:03,934
was just one of many shows he was on.

171
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:07,730
I'm sorry.

172
00:11:08,856 --> 00:11:10,733
I shouldn't have vented like this.

173
00:11:11,317 --> 00:11:12,443
It's okay.

174
00:11:13,611 --> 00:11:17,364
Do you know about Mr. Amagi
having a pre-existing medical condition?

175
00:11:17,448 --> 00:11:18,824
No, nothing in particular.

176
00:11:19,825 --> 00:11:21,035
I see.

177
00:11:26,916 --> 00:11:28,626
What is this?

178
00:11:29,335 --> 00:11:30,669
Oh.

179
00:11:30,753 --> 00:11:33,047
It's the broadcast records
for the past 20 years.

180
00:11:33,130 --> 00:11:35,132
It's for the memorial special.

181
00:11:35,216 --> 00:11:36,675
May I take a look at it?

182
00:11:36,759 --> 00:11:37,885
Go ahead.

183
00:11:41,514 --> 00:11:43,724
He was always doing as he pleased.

184
00:11:47,603 --> 00:11:49,647
What happened
during this particular month?

185
00:11:50,231 --> 00:11:51,148
Pardon?

186
00:11:52,316 --> 00:11:54,985
This is a regularly scheduled
live broadcast, correct?

187
00:11:55,069 --> 00:11:59,156
He suddenly demanded
an extended leave of absence.

188
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:02,284
It was pretty tough
trying to fill it up with recaps.

189
00:12:04,537 --> 00:12:07,915
2021 JUNE 5TH - NO BROADCAST
JUNE 12-26 RECAP EPISODES

190
00:12:08,749 --> 00:12:09,833
Mr. Muto.

191
00:12:09,917 --> 00:12:11,043
Yes?

192
00:12:11,126 --> 00:12:12,545
What are you doing?

193
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:16,423
We need you
to finish the script structure quickly.

194
00:12:16,507 --> 00:12:18,968
Oh, right.

195
00:12:19,051 --> 00:12:20,886
Sorry, we know you're busy.

196
00:12:20,970 --> 00:12:22,721
Thank you very much.

197
00:12:22,805 --> 00:12:25,975
Twenty years of consistent broadcasting
is truly impressive.

198
00:12:28,852 --> 00:12:31,146
The writers are waiting for you.

199
00:12:32,189 --> 00:12:33,649
Excuse me.

200
00:12:51,041 --> 00:12:54,295
Things disappear so often
at TV stations, don't they?

201
00:12:54,378 --> 00:12:56,922
There are always so many
people coming and going.

202
00:12:57,006 --> 00:12:59,592
Even a suitcase went missing recently.

203
00:12:59,675 --> 00:13:00,926
Excuse me.

204
00:13:02,303 --> 00:13:04,263
May I have one of these?

205
00:13:04,346 --> 00:13:05,347
What?

206
00:13:05,431 --> 00:13:07,349
Sliced melon is my absolute favorite.

207
00:13:08,142 --> 00:13:09,059
Go ahead.

208
00:13:09,143 --> 00:13:11,020
Thank you very much.

209
00:13:11,103 --> 00:13:12,396
Sorry.

210
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:26,118
This is…

211
00:13:27,244 --> 00:13:28,495
Love-chan.

212
00:13:28,579 --> 00:13:29,455
LOVE-CHAN'S BIG ADVENTURE

213
00:13:31,624 --> 00:13:34,126
I adore this character.

214
00:13:36,503 --> 00:13:37,504
Love-chan.

215
00:13:46,513 --> 00:13:48,682
AMAGI

216
00:13:48,766 --> 00:13:54,480
Did Mr. Amagi ever seem troubled
or stressed about his work?

217
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,690
No, not particularly.

218
00:13:59,943 --> 00:14:03,364
Were you also present at the venue
on that day?

219
00:14:05,991 --> 00:14:08,702
Did he keep his plans
in a schedule or anything?

220
00:14:08,786 --> 00:14:10,371
Oh, yes.

221
00:14:10,913 --> 00:14:12,289
May we take a look at it?

222
00:14:14,416 --> 00:14:15,459
Sure.

223
00:14:21,882 --> 00:14:22,800
Here you go.

224
00:14:22,883 --> 00:14:24,218
Thank you very much.

225
00:14:33,894 --> 00:14:37,189
He was an extraordinarily
meticulous person, wasn't he?

226
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:40,734
He broke his schedule down
into 30-minute blocks.

227
00:14:41,485 --> 00:14:44,738
He disciplined himself strictly
to prepare for the live broadcasts.

228
00:14:47,533 --> 00:14:50,619
Running, yoga, even reading.

229
00:14:55,207 --> 00:14:57,710
What's this time written in red?

230
00:14:58,836 --> 00:14:59,837
What?

231
00:15:01,171 --> 00:15:02,214
This.

232
00:15:07,302 --> 00:15:10,389
I believe my husband
was simply keeping a record

233
00:15:10,472 --> 00:15:12,391
of the days he couldn't finish on time.

234
00:15:14,309 --> 00:15:16,353
He was a man of very particular habits.

235
00:15:21,692 --> 00:15:23,235
I see.

236
00:15:23,986 --> 00:15:27,072
Thank you for speaking with us
during such a difficult time.

237
00:15:32,369 --> 00:15:35,414
To think he managed his life
with that much stoicism…

238
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:40,169
Living life in 30-minute increments…

239
00:15:42,379 --> 00:15:45,049
It must have been difficult
for Yuka as well.

240
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:54,725
He may have had a side to him
that he never showed to anyone.

241
00:16:23,587 --> 00:16:26,715
TAKASAKA FAMILY GRAVE

242
00:16:39,937 --> 00:16:42,689
INCOMING CALL

243
00:16:47,152 --> 00:16:49,154
PRIVATE CALLER

244
00:16:59,248 --> 00:17:00,290
I'm back.

245
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:06,255
Regarding Mr. Amagi,
no poison was detected in the body.

246
00:17:06,338 --> 00:17:08,006
Really?

247
00:17:09,716 --> 00:17:10,884
Thank you.

248
00:17:12,344 --> 00:17:13,971
I'm back.

249
00:17:16,682 --> 00:17:18,475
What are you looking at?

250
00:17:18,559 --> 00:17:20,644
Surveillance camera footage from that day.

251
00:17:20,727 --> 00:17:23,772
Igawa gave it to us, hoping
it might help with the investigation.

252
00:17:24,606 --> 00:17:25,649
Excuse me.

253
00:17:27,526 --> 00:17:31,572
ROOF CAMERA

254
00:17:32,656 --> 00:17:36,785
I believe Mr. Muto discovers
his friend's body shortly after this.

255
00:17:36,869 --> 00:17:39,454
Could you show me that one more time?

256
00:17:39,538 --> 00:17:40,414
Yes.

257
00:17:50,257 --> 00:17:53,010
YUSATA'S 20TH ANNIVERSARY CELEBRATION

258
00:18:02,936 --> 00:18:04,146
Is something wrong?

259
00:18:09,026 --> 00:18:11,570
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

260
00:18:11,653 --> 00:18:13,197
<i>Hello, this is Igawa.</i>

261
00:18:13,739 --> 00:18:17,534
Oh. Thank you for the surveillance
camera footage earlier--

262
00:18:18,869 --> 00:18:19,703
What?

263
00:18:20,913 --> 00:18:23,916
Yuka attempted suicide?

264
00:18:26,043 --> 00:18:27,169
What?

265
00:18:30,797 --> 00:18:34,968
She survived,
but she hasn't regained consciousness yet.

266
00:18:39,097 --> 00:18:40,390
I understand.

267
00:18:41,725 --> 00:18:43,227
Thank you very much.

268
00:18:48,899 --> 00:18:51,652
They said she overdosed on sleeping pills.

269
00:18:57,032 --> 00:18:58,325
Dr. Masumi.

270
00:18:58,992 --> 00:19:01,328
Regarding the skull fracture marks
you asked about,

271
00:19:01,411 --> 00:19:03,747
we found out they are
from over five years ago.

272
00:19:05,666 --> 00:19:08,627
MEDICAL REPORT
KOICHI AMAGI

273
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:12,089
Could this have something to do
with the case?

274
00:19:12,589 --> 00:19:13,465
Dr. Takamori.

275
00:19:13,548 --> 00:19:17,844
Could you check if anything has
gone missing inside the station recently?

276
00:19:18,679 --> 00:19:19,596
Yes.

277
00:19:24,643 --> 00:19:27,187
OVERVIEW

278
00:19:31,275 --> 00:19:35,320
I would like to talk to you about
the long-term leave from five years ago.

279
00:19:35,404 --> 00:19:37,364
Is this about Amagi again?

280
00:19:38,073 --> 00:19:39,992
Mr. Amagi's skull had fracture marks

281
00:19:40,075 --> 00:19:43,829
believed to have occurred
about five years ago.

282
00:19:45,747 --> 00:19:48,583
Is there anything at all
you might have noticed?

283
00:19:49,167 --> 00:19:52,004
Maybe in the past I would have,
but not recently, no.

284
00:19:53,714 --> 00:19:56,133
These days he wouldn't even
show up for meetings,

285
00:19:56,216 --> 00:19:58,468
and when he did,
he was always checking the time.

286
00:20:00,554 --> 00:20:01,596
There was a time

287
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:04,683
when he cared about the program
more than anyone, though.

288
00:20:06,268 --> 00:20:08,478
How about this for the next segment?

289
00:20:08,562 --> 00:20:11,064
Really? You brought another one?

290
00:20:13,442 --> 00:20:15,235
Sorry, but I'm busy.

291
00:20:25,954 --> 00:20:27,122
Excuse me.

292
00:20:30,042 --> 00:20:33,086
Didn't we meet
in the editing room the other day?

293
00:20:33,587 --> 00:20:34,629
Right.

294
00:20:35,797 --> 00:20:39,801
There is a possibility that the period
when Mr. Amagi took his long-term leave

295
00:20:39,885 --> 00:20:42,846
matches the timing
of the fracture found on his skull.

296
00:20:44,973 --> 00:20:48,226
Do you happen to know anything about it?

297
00:20:54,024 --> 00:20:56,443
I thought I would have
to tell someone eventually.

298
00:20:58,028 --> 00:20:59,571
Five years ago,

299
00:21:00,572 --> 00:21:02,824
I was the one
who caused Mr. Amagi's injury.

300
00:21:05,035 --> 00:21:06,078
What?

301
00:21:06,661 --> 00:21:07,829
Back then,

302
00:21:07,913 --> 00:21:10,207
<i>I was still just a new director.</i>

303
00:21:10,290 --> 00:21:12,292
<i>I was working for days, without sleeping.</i>

304
00:21:13,668 --> 00:21:15,170
<i>I was totally out of it.</i>

305
00:21:24,679 --> 00:21:25,972
I'm sorry!

306
00:21:26,556 --> 00:21:27,682
I'm fine.

307
00:21:27,766 --> 00:21:29,142
No, but…

308
00:21:29,226 --> 00:21:30,936
-What happened?
-I'm really fine.

309
00:21:31,019 --> 00:21:32,312
I'm sorry, I was careless…

310
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:33,897
-You okay?
-Don't worry!

311
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:35,190
Don't worry.

312
00:21:37,609 --> 00:21:39,569
A light just tipped over.

313
00:21:45,409 --> 00:21:48,495
At the time, our ratings were stagnant,

314
00:21:49,204 --> 00:21:52,416
and the show was
on the chopping block for cancellation.

315
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:54,751
So,

316
00:21:55,585 --> 00:21:57,212
we kept it a secret.

317
00:21:59,923 --> 00:22:04,302
So the fracture marks on his head
were caused by that accident.

318
00:22:04,886 --> 00:22:05,887
Yes.

319
00:22:05,971 --> 00:22:09,391
Did Mr. Muto really not know about it?

320
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:12,978
I don't think he knew about the fracture.

321
00:22:15,397 --> 00:22:16,731
I see.

322
00:22:21,278 --> 00:22:26,908
So the skull fracture marks
were from an accident that was covered up.

323
00:22:31,163 --> 00:22:32,080
Hello?

324
00:22:33,999 --> 00:22:35,167
What?

325
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:36,209
Really?

326
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:40,046
Yuka has regained consciousness.

327
00:22:41,423 --> 00:22:42,841
I will go check on her.

328
00:22:42,924 --> 00:22:43,925
Okay.

329
00:22:44,009 --> 00:22:45,427
I will stay here a little longer.

330
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:46,511
Right, okay.

331
00:22:47,512 --> 00:22:49,514
May I come visit now?

332
00:22:55,562 --> 00:22:56,646
Excuse me.

333
00:22:56,730 --> 00:22:59,691
I am Masumi
from the Medical Examiner's office.

334
00:22:59,774 --> 00:23:00,817
Yes?

335
00:23:00,901 --> 00:23:04,571
Did Mr. Amagi come here often?

336
00:23:05,155 --> 00:23:06,114
Yes.

337
00:23:06,198 --> 00:23:10,160
Ever since <i>Yusata </i>started, he has always
stopped by before the live broadcast.

338
00:23:11,036 --> 00:23:12,621
Around what time would that be?

339
00:23:12,704 --> 00:23:16,791
He would come to get water
30 minutes before the broadcast.

340
00:23:17,459 --> 00:23:21,046
I guess even a star gets nervous
before a live broadcast, right?

341
00:23:21,588 --> 00:23:25,675
Especially him, since he cared about
his routine more than anyone.

342
00:23:37,187 --> 00:23:41,149
I'm sorry for suddenly
asking so many questions

343
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:45,195
when we visited the other day.

344
00:23:49,908 --> 00:23:52,577
I'm glad you are safe.

345
00:24:02,963 --> 00:24:07,842
I used to watch Mr. Amagi's show
often at this time.

346
00:24:09,678 --> 00:24:13,181
He always looked so happy on screen.

347
00:24:15,433 --> 00:24:17,978
When I watched him,

348
00:24:18,937 --> 00:24:22,607
it made the fatigue of the week
melt away a little.

349
00:24:28,989 --> 00:24:29,823
But,

350
00:24:31,408 --> 00:24:32,659
I think…

351
00:24:34,828 --> 00:24:37,038
he had many hardships going on

352
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:45,297
that we as viewers never knew about.

353
00:24:50,927 --> 00:24:52,220
And I think that,

354
00:24:53,346 --> 00:24:55,015
for decades,

355
00:24:56,558 --> 00:24:59,311
he was able to give so much joy to people…

356
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:04,899
because you were there for him.

357
00:25:10,905 --> 00:25:11,865
Actually…

358
00:25:18,621 --> 00:25:20,165
Sorry to call you.

359
00:25:21,124 --> 00:25:22,959
Regarding MEJ,

360
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:26,755
you know how the prosecution
feels about them, right?

361
00:25:26,838 --> 00:25:27,714
MINISTRY OF HEALTH, LABOR AND WELFARE

362
00:25:27,797 --> 00:25:31,509
I understand. I will have someone
look into the internal affairs of MEJ.

363
00:25:33,762 --> 00:25:36,973
You truly are a smart person,
Mr. Yamazaki.

364
00:25:39,017 --> 00:25:39,851
Okay.

365
00:25:41,061 --> 00:25:43,730
I will report back as soon as I find out.

366
00:26:02,874 --> 00:26:05,001
Is that from the anniversary celebration?

367
00:26:05,085 --> 00:26:06,252
Oh, yes.

368
00:26:07,879 --> 00:26:09,255
What video is that?

369
00:26:09,964 --> 00:26:11,883
Live stream footage from the party.

370
00:26:11,966 --> 00:26:14,427
<i>We're at the </i>Yusata <i>party!</i>

371
00:26:15,220 --> 00:26:19,432
It hurts to think that at this time,
he might have died already.

372
00:26:20,225 --> 00:26:23,520
<i>"Is Mr. Amagi there, too?"</i>

373
00:26:28,233 --> 00:26:29,359
Dr. Masumi.

374
00:26:29,442 --> 00:26:31,319
I received this from Yuka.

375
00:26:32,695 --> 00:26:33,988
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

376
00:26:37,617 --> 00:26:40,537
Dr. Takamori, do you have
the station's lost and found list?

377
00:26:43,915 --> 00:26:45,250
Here it is.

378
00:26:50,505 --> 00:26:52,340
LIGHT BLUE SUITCASE

379
00:27:00,974 --> 00:27:03,143
It is believed he fell from over there.

380
00:27:03,226 --> 00:27:05,645
<i>There are numerous linear marks…</i>

381
00:27:05,728 --> 00:27:07,105
<i>…bite wound.</i>

382
00:27:07,689 --> 00:27:10,608
<i>He broke his schedule down</i>
<i>into 30-minute blocks.</i>

383
00:27:10,692 --> 00:27:12,694
What's this time written in red?

384
00:27:12,777 --> 00:27:14,362
My husband was simply keeping a record

385
00:27:14,446 --> 00:27:16,114
of the days he couldn't finish on time.

386
00:27:16,197 --> 00:27:17,866
He was always just checking the time.

387
00:27:19,242 --> 00:27:22,662
He would come to get water
30 minutes before the broadcast.

388
00:27:22,745 --> 00:27:24,038
Five years ago,

389
00:27:24,122 --> 00:27:26,166
<i>I was the one</i>
<i>who caused Mr. Amagi's injury.</i>

390
00:27:26,249 --> 00:27:28,751
<i>I don't think he knew about the fracture.</i>

391
00:27:30,462 --> 00:27:33,089
Things disappear so often
at TV stations, don't they?

392
00:27:33,173 --> 00:27:36,217
Even a suitcase went missing recently.

393
00:27:36,301 --> 00:27:39,679
I believe Mr. Muto discovers
his friend's body shortly after this.

394
00:27:42,056 --> 00:27:45,602
<i>It is as if only the interior of the body</i>
<i>experienced the fall.</i>

395
00:27:59,574 --> 00:28:01,075
The pieces may be…

396
00:28:02,285 --> 00:28:04,078
coming together.

397
00:28:07,916 --> 00:28:11,252
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

398
00:28:26,184 --> 00:28:29,020
Oh. I'm sorry.
I know you're busy, Mr. Muto.

399
00:28:29,604 --> 00:28:31,773
What did you want to talk about?

400
00:28:31,856 --> 00:28:35,860
According to the autopsy,
the cause of Mr. Amagi's death

401
00:28:35,944 --> 00:28:39,572
was traumatic shock
from a fall from a high place.

402
00:28:41,074 --> 00:28:41,991
However,

403
00:28:42,075 --> 00:28:46,120
what struck me as highly unusual
was how clean the body was.

404
00:28:48,998 --> 00:28:54,712
There were far too few external injuries
for a fall from such a height.

405
00:28:54,796 --> 00:28:57,924
It was almost as if
he was being protected by something.

406
00:29:00,301 --> 00:29:01,511
Furthermore,

407
00:29:01,594 --> 00:29:05,431
Mr. Amagi's body had linear abrasions

408
00:29:05,515 --> 00:29:08,685
that could not have been
caused by jumping.

409
00:29:10,478 --> 00:29:11,646
Linear abrasions?

410
00:29:11,729 --> 00:29:12,730
Yes.

411
00:29:14,148 --> 00:29:18,736
The kind you get when rolling down
a flight of stairs, for instance.

412
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:21,990
In other words,

413
00:29:22,073 --> 00:29:25,535
Amagi was involved in a separate incident

414
00:29:25,618 --> 00:29:28,955
before his fall from a higher location.

415
00:29:37,297 --> 00:29:39,716
You'll be fine even if I'm gone, right?

416
00:29:40,633 --> 00:29:41,551
What?

417
00:29:44,637 --> 00:29:46,180
I'm at my limit.

418
00:29:52,270 --> 00:29:54,147
If that's a joke, it's not funny.

419
00:30:01,696 --> 00:30:04,032
Why now, of all times?

420
00:30:12,165 --> 00:30:13,333
What's the reason?

421
00:30:21,257 --> 00:30:22,342
Fine.

422
00:30:23,760 --> 00:30:25,011
Let's go somewhere else.

423
00:30:27,805 --> 00:30:28,681
Hey!

424
00:30:28,765 --> 00:30:30,892
YUSATA 20TH ANNIVERSARY
CELEBRATION VENUE

425
00:30:30,975 --> 00:30:31,893
Hey.

426
00:30:31,976 --> 00:30:33,853
You just got tired of it, didn't you?

427
00:30:35,063 --> 00:30:36,606
Must be nice for you.

428
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:40,693
You'll have plenty of work
even if <i>Yusata </i>gets canceled.

429
00:30:44,072 --> 00:30:46,115
Just because you got a little famous…

430
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,745
Say something.

431
00:30:51,746 --> 00:30:53,039
Whoa, hey!

432
00:30:56,334 --> 00:30:58,878
Hey!

433
00:30:58,962 --> 00:31:00,797
Hey!

434
00:31:05,802 --> 00:31:08,137
H-He's dead…

435
00:31:08,221 --> 00:31:10,098
Because those linear abrasions

436
00:31:10,181 --> 00:31:13,518
were not present
during the evening live broadcast,

437
00:31:14,102 --> 00:31:17,939
we believe they were sustained
during the celebration party.

438
00:31:20,149 --> 00:31:22,527
You were the first to find him,

439
00:31:22,610 --> 00:31:26,864
and we were told you rushed over
immediately upon hearing a sound.

440
00:31:27,740 --> 00:31:31,494
While your actions
were captured on security footage,

441
00:31:31,577 --> 00:31:35,123
the direction you headed raises questions.

442
00:31:37,417 --> 00:31:39,585
Why did you go out of your way
to take a detour

443
00:31:39,669 --> 00:31:41,921
to reach the spot where he fell?

444
00:31:42,547 --> 00:31:43,423
That's because--

445
00:31:43,506 --> 00:31:46,634
If you truly rushed over
the moment you heard the sound,

446
00:31:47,260 --> 00:31:49,512
then this behavior

447
00:31:50,263 --> 00:31:51,639
doesn't add up.

448
00:31:53,558 --> 00:31:56,060
Everyone, let's move inside for now!

449
00:31:56,144 --> 00:31:58,104
Sorry, follow me please!

450
00:31:59,439 --> 00:32:01,566
Please be careful! It's slippery.

451
00:32:04,068 --> 00:32:04,902
Excuse me!

452
00:32:05,903 --> 00:32:07,030
I'm very sorry!

453
00:32:15,371 --> 00:32:20,626
A large suitcase has gone missing
from this television station.

454
00:32:20,710 --> 00:32:23,796
<i>Even a suitcase went missing recently.</i>

455
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:28,426
Given that the celebration party
was underway that day,

456
00:32:28,926 --> 00:32:30,970
you hid Mr. Amagi

457
00:32:31,929 --> 00:32:33,556
inside that suitcase

458
00:32:34,932 --> 00:32:38,686
<i>to keep him out of sight, didn't you?</i>

459
00:32:44,317 --> 00:32:47,737
The missing suitcase
can actually be spotted

460
00:32:47,820 --> 00:32:50,740
in a video that was being
live-streamed during the party.

461
00:32:51,574 --> 00:32:52,450
For some reason,

462
00:32:53,034 --> 00:32:56,621
you are seen in it
pushing the suitcase in from outside.

463
00:33:00,291 --> 00:33:01,626
Furthermore,

464
00:33:01,709 --> 00:33:05,505
there's a mark on the ground that only
something angular could have made.

465
00:33:06,923 --> 00:33:09,467
When you put all those pieces together,

466
00:33:10,051 --> 00:33:14,931
it appears Amagi fell
while he was still inside that suitcase.

467
00:33:16,432 --> 00:33:18,392
Doesn't it seem that way?

468
00:33:27,568 --> 00:33:29,695
I never intended to kill him.

469
00:33:31,531 --> 00:33:32,615
I only tried

470
00:33:33,324 --> 00:33:36,702
to make him turn around on the stairs.

471
00:33:38,162 --> 00:33:39,288
But then,

472
00:33:41,082 --> 00:33:42,500
he just collapsed so easily.

473
00:33:47,338 --> 00:33:49,715
And the suitcase, too…

474
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:56,639
I didn't intentionally drop it.

475
00:33:57,682 --> 00:33:59,183
It moved on its own.

476
00:33:59,267 --> 00:34:02,937
Mr. Amagi's hands showed absolutely
no signs of defensive wounds.

477
00:34:04,272 --> 00:34:05,189
What?

478
00:34:05,273 --> 00:34:08,109
This indicates that
he fell down the stairs

479
00:34:08,192 --> 00:34:11,737
without being able
to reflexively break his fall.

480
00:34:16,450 --> 00:34:22,456
We believe he was experiencing
a specific medical episode at that moment.

481
00:34:23,583 --> 00:34:26,252
One that leaves bite marks
on the side of the tongue.

482
00:34:26,335 --> 00:34:27,295
It was…

483
00:34:28,963 --> 00:34:30,256
epilepsy.

484
00:34:32,049 --> 00:34:33,134
Epilepsy?

485
00:34:35,136 --> 00:34:36,721
Must be nice for you.

486
00:34:37,513 --> 00:34:40,641
You'll have plenty of work
even if <i>Yusata </i>gets canceled.

487
00:34:47,732 --> 00:34:49,692
Traumatic epilepsy.

488
00:34:51,027 --> 00:34:52,528
It is a chronic condition

489
00:34:52,612 --> 00:34:55,865
that manifests when the brain
is damaged from a prior head injury.

490
00:34:56,574 --> 00:34:59,535
Mr. Amagi had been suffering
from traumatic epilepsy

491
00:34:59,619 --> 00:35:02,288
<i>ever since an accident five years ago.</i>

492
00:35:05,124 --> 00:35:09,170
This is the anti-epileptic medication
he was taking.

493
00:35:11,547 --> 00:35:15,635
The reason the suitcase moved
on its own on the roof is likely

494
00:35:15,718 --> 00:35:22,475
because Mr. Amagi regained consciousness
from his epileptic seizure.

495
00:35:42,620 --> 00:35:43,996
What the…

496
00:35:45,164 --> 00:35:48,334
Ever since that original accident,

497
00:35:48,417 --> 00:35:51,295
<i>he apparently kept track of time</i>
<i>meticulously</i>

498
00:35:51,379 --> 00:35:55,383
solely to manage his seizure patterns
and his response plan.

499
00:36:00,513 --> 00:36:01,847
What is all this about?

500
00:36:01,931 --> 00:36:03,349
I believe Mr. Amagi

501
00:36:04,225 --> 00:36:06,394
wanted to keep it a secret.

502
00:36:07,186 --> 00:36:09,438
So that you would never find out.

503
00:36:11,315 --> 00:36:12,316
What?

504
00:36:12,817 --> 00:36:16,779
INTERNAL MEDICINE
KOICHI AMAGI

505
00:36:16,862 --> 00:36:18,155
Five years ago,

506
00:36:19,699 --> 00:36:21,993
my husband developed epilepsy

507
00:36:23,452 --> 00:36:25,454
as the result of an accident.

508
00:36:28,374 --> 00:36:30,501
He made it a rule to take his medicine

509
00:36:30,584 --> 00:36:33,838
30 minutes before going on air,
almost like a protective ritual.

510
00:36:38,551 --> 00:36:39,844
I see.

511
00:36:43,806 --> 00:36:46,767
But why keep it a secret between you two?

512
00:36:49,729 --> 00:36:53,691
Couldn't he have leaned
on other people for help?

513
00:36:56,402 --> 00:36:59,363
My husband insisted on doing it that way.

514
00:37:01,699 --> 00:37:04,035
He said if his epilepsy
became public knowledge,

515
00:37:04,118 --> 00:37:06,162
people would dig into the root cause,

516
00:37:07,747 --> 00:37:10,750
and that could lead to
an investigation of the show itself.

517
00:37:12,501 --> 00:37:15,546
Don't you think it's time you retired?

518
00:37:16,839 --> 00:37:19,425
Your seizures have been
getting more frequent lately,

519
00:37:19,508 --> 00:37:21,135
and your body is at its limit.

520
00:37:23,429 --> 00:37:24,805
Just a little longer.

521
00:37:26,015 --> 00:37:26,891
But…

522
00:37:26,974 --> 00:37:28,309
Twenty years.

523
00:37:30,186 --> 00:37:33,481
I really want to make sure Muto
gets his moment in the spotlight.

524
00:37:36,067 --> 00:37:39,945
We built this show together from the days
when we were complete nobodies.

525
00:37:41,364 --> 00:37:42,782
This is a critical time.

526
00:37:44,116 --> 00:37:46,952
We live in an era
where shows get canceled easily,

527
00:37:47,036 --> 00:37:49,663
and everyone is working so hard
to turn things around.

528
00:37:52,666 --> 00:37:54,919
I know I'm asking a lot of you, but…

529
00:38:08,724 --> 00:38:11,519
The reason he distanced himself
from the production

530
00:38:11,602 --> 00:38:14,146
and was always obsessing over the time

531
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:20,152
was to protect the show that held so many
special memories for you both.

532
00:38:23,322 --> 00:38:26,242
Even then, why…?

533
00:38:28,369 --> 00:38:30,955
Likely because if you knew
about his illness

534
00:38:31,789 --> 00:38:34,583
he thought you'd put an end to the show.

535
00:38:38,587 --> 00:38:41,841
You are a deeply responsible person,

536
00:38:41,924 --> 00:38:45,886
and Mr. Amagi knew that
better than anyone, after all.

537
00:38:49,682 --> 00:38:53,060
You're too intense, working on
these ideas until morning.

538
00:38:54,061 --> 00:38:56,480
On the very day
of the live broadcast, no less.

539
00:39:01,193 --> 00:39:03,404
His wife said
that right up until his death,

540
00:39:04,155 --> 00:39:07,867
he talked about nothing but you
whenever he was at home.

541
00:39:12,079 --> 00:39:15,958
That's because you waste
way too much time chatting.

542
00:39:17,418 --> 00:39:19,462
And you always make it worse.

543
00:39:20,087 --> 00:39:24,091
-How about this for the next segment?
-Really? You brought another one?

544
00:39:24,592 --> 00:39:25,926
You don't quit.

545
00:39:27,178 --> 00:39:28,179
<i>What do you think?</i>

546
00:39:29,680 --> 00:39:30,681
<i>It's great.</i>

547
00:39:31,182 --> 00:39:32,683
<i>-Isn't it?</i>
<i>-Yeah.</i>

548
00:39:36,645 --> 00:39:40,941
YUSATA SEGMENT IDEAS

549
00:39:49,909 --> 00:39:53,996
The reason he hid his illness
until he passed away

550
00:39:54,872 --> 00:39:56,999
was to protect the time he spent with you,

551
00:39:57,708 --> 00:40:01,754
which was more important
than anything else.

552
00:40:04,965 --> 00:40:10,638
I hope we can continue this show forever.

553
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:55,284
20 YEARS OF GOODBYES ARE
A "THANK YOU" SPOKEN WITH LOVE

554
00:42:00,581 --> 00:42:01,999
I'm finished!

555
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:05,836
Hey!

556
00:42:05,919 --> 00:42:07,129
Look, look!

557
00:42:07,796 --> 00:42:09,214
What happened?

558
00:42:11,133 --> 00:42:12,009
This is…

559
00:42:12,593 --> 00:42:14,553
<i>I'm Suzuki from Orient Daily.</i>

560
00:42:14,637 --> 00:42:17,848
<i>Could you tell us what</i>
<i>has come to light during this case?</i>

561
00:42:19,475 --> 00:42:21,977
They're saying MEJ probed into the truth.

562
00:42:22,061 --> 00:42:23,771
That makes me feel kind of proud.

563
00:42:23,854 --> 00:42:27,399
It's rare for forensic scientists
to get this much attention.

564
00:42:28,734 --> 00:42:30,444
Wow, that's amazing.

565
00:42:30,527 --> 00:42:32,571
Cool, huh?

566
00:42:32,655 --> 00:42:34,198
I'm back.

567
00:42:34,281 --> 00:42:35,991
-Hey!
-Welcome back!

568
00:42:36,075 --> 00:42:38,327
I'm back and I brought souvenirs.

569
00:42:38,410 --> 00:42:39,286
Oh, thank you.

570
00:42:39,370 --> 00:42:40,287
Thanks.

571
00:42:40,371 --> 00:42:41,372
Thank you.

572
00:42:42,206 --> 00:42:43,332
Dr. Masumi.

573
00:42:43,415 --> 00:42:44,291
Here.

574
00:42:44,375 --> 00:42:45,709
Your souvenir.

575
00:42:45,793 --> 00:42:47,002
LIMITED KYOTO EDITION

576
00:42:47,086 --> 00:42:48,587
Thank you very much.

577
00:42:49,463 --> 00:42:50,756
Welcome back.

578
00:42:52,966 --> 00:42:54,134
Thank you.

579
00:42:55,219 --> 00:42:58,222
-Hey, look at this, Dr. Masumi.
-What?

580
00:42:58,305 --> 00:43:00,349
MEJ is getting attention!

581
00:43:17,408 --> 00:43:18,742
ANOTHER STRANGLED BODY FOUND IN SHIRAMINE

582
00:43:18,826 --> 00:43:19,868
THE CITY IS ON ALERT

583
00:43:19,952 --> 00:43:21,620
GUARD SENT AROUND SHIRAMINE

584
00:43:31,171 --> 00:43:35,259
<i>I believe many people have learned about</i>
<i>MEJ for the first time through this event,</i>

585
00:43:35,342 --> 00:43:37,720
<i>but could you explain once again</i>
<i>what kind of system it is?</i>

586
00:43:37,803 --> 00:43:40,723
<i>What was the deciding factor</i>
<i>in uncovering the truth?</i>

587
00:43:43,183 --> 00:43:47,187
<i>The American system has been implemented,</i>
<i>but have you felt any resistance?</i>

588
00:43:52,901 --> 00:43:56,029
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.

589
00:43:56,029 --> 00:43:57,029
MkvDrama.net

